      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- The Plane of Knowledge [zone=158]\n**Who:**\n- Heretic Drahur [ _Necromancer Spells 1-25_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 60\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Spell\n**Quest Items:**\n- Ethereal Parchment [item=16329]\n- Glyphed Rune Word [item=16562]\n- Spectral Parchment [item=16493]\n**Era:** | !Planes of Power\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- Necromancer\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 7 21:02:12 2002\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | You say, 'Hail, Heretic Drahur'\nHeretic Drahur says 'Salutations. The keepers of necromancy in New Tanaan are neither your enemy or foe, as they may have been upon the material world of Norrath. Though our natures are in tact, we have elevated ourselves beyond the petty, debased bickering that Norrath has come to embody over the passing eras. All adventurers and intelligent beings are welcome in our midst, for we share only the common goal of knowledge and personal betterment in our power. I have gathered tomes and spells that I no longer have use for, as I have ascended beyond Norrath's limitations of the dark arts. However, you remain a mortal still and your abilities may never reach the esteemed levels of ours, bur do not let this discourage you. Search my tomes and perhaps I hold something of importance or relevance to your current quest for power. There is another realm of magic that I am quite familiar with, as well -- the aspects of planar magic.'\n_Bring Drahur various parchments for PoP spells in return._\n_Ethereal Parchments will yield you 61-62nd level spells._\n_Spectral Parchments will yield you 63-64th level spells._\n_Glyphed Rune Words will yield you 65th level spells._\nHeretic Drahur takes the arcane item from you. The erudite inspects the incorporeal item for a brief amount of time. He then closes his eyes and begins a dark chant that causes the air about you to grow cold and stiff - your breathing is briefly impaired and for a single moment, you feel as if you are about to suffocate. As the erudite's voice falls back to silence, the discomfort fades and you look upon the item in his hands. It is corporeal now - tangible in all aspects. Runes of inky black have formed upon the item - runes that you recognize immediately as those of necromantic foundations. The erudite gives a gentle nod of his head and hands the scroll to you, 'This should prove more than useful for your endeavors in the planes. However, it extends beyond such limits and can be applied to the primordial world.'\n- Spell: Blood of Thule [item=16959]\n- Spell: Child of Bertoxxulous [item=16960]\n- Spell: Dark Plague [item=16948]\n- Spell: Death's Silence [item=16954]\n- Spell: Destroy Undead [item=16878]\n- Spell: Eidolon Bellow [Dark Reign]\n- Spell: Eidolon Bellow [Norrath's Keepers]\n- Spell: Embracing Darkness [item=16955]\n- Spell: Force Shield [item=16956]\n- Spell: Greater Immobilize [item=16705]\n- Spell: Legacy of Zek [item=16949]\n- Spell: Neurotoxin [item=16950]\n- Spell: Petrifying Earth [item=16718]\n- Spell: Rune of Death [item=16952]\n- Spell: Saryrn's Companion [item=16957]\n- Spell: Saryrn's Kiss [item=16953]\n- Spell: Seduction of Saryrn [item=16958]\n- Spell: Shield of Maelin [item=16622]\n- Spell: Shield of the Arcane [item=16605]\n- Spell: Touch of Death [item=55925]\n- Spell: Touch of Mujaki [item=16951]\n- Spell: Unholy Bellow [Dark Reign]\n- Spell: Unholy Bellow [Norrath's Keepers]\n- Spell: Word of Terris [item=16961]",
